! REPRODUCER, not a test: strap_asm.py refuses a floating-point constant
! whose fraction is zero.  Found 2026-11-15 transcribing C22-6578
! Chapter 3 (docs/NEXT.md, "C22-6578 CHAPTER 3").
!
!   python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'strap'); \
!     from strap_asm import assemble; \
!     assemble(open('decks/problem_3_dd_zero_fraction.strap').read())"
!
!   AssemblerError: line N: DD(N) literal '0.0X48' is zero, which is not
!   implemented (no listed example)
!
! THERE ARE LISTED EXAMPLES.  All read in the ink:
!   C22-6578 printed p.26, Problems 3.1 and 3.2:
!       X48     DD(N), 0.0X48           'binary exponent of 48
!   C22-6578 printed p.28-29, Problem 3.4:
!       A       DD(N), 0.0              'lower limit
!       ANS     DD(N), 0
!   Reference Manual printed p.103, Figure 33:
!       CON1    DD (N), +0E +48
!
! The host STRAP II (ASM=strap2) assembles all three: X48 is
! 0600000000000000 (exponent 48, a zero fraction: C28-6129 printed p.27,
! "EXPONENT ENTRY ... overrules and replaces the exponent computed by
! STRAP"), and the other two are words of zero bits.  The page's own
! comment says what X48 is for -- "forces the fraction of N to shift
! right the proper amount" -- so the exponent is the whole of the
! constant and a zero fraction is its point.
!
! decks/problem_3_1.strap runs the first on the model under ASM=strap2.

START   BEW, $
X48     DD(N), 0.0X48
A       DD(N), 0.0
ANS     DD(N), 0
        END, START
